text:
Mira: quick heads-up — PR #4821 updates the /v1/chat/completions messages schema. I'm proposing `tool_args` become an optional top-level map on the message object instead of nested under `tool_call.payload`. Need a compatibility sanity-check before I merge.
Sam: pinged. can you paste the minimal before/after?
Mira: before:```json
{
  "message": {
    "role": "assistant",
    "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "..."}],
    "tool_call": {
      "name": "search",
      "payload": { "q": "x" }
    }
  }
}
``` after (proposed):```json
{
  "message": {
    "role": "assistant",
    "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "..."}],
    "tool_call": {
      "name": "search"
    },
    "tool_args": { "q": "x" }  // optional
  }
}
```
Mira: rationale: separates invocation metadata from the args so streaming deltas can emit `tool_call` early and args can be populated later (helps low-latency routing).
Jon: interesting. two quick checks from me: 1) how do SDKs that deserialize to typed models handle missing `tool_args`? 2) fallback when args arrive after the stream end?
Mira: good points. proposal: SDKs treat `tool_args` as optional map defaulting to null/{}. For streaming we add an explicit `event: \"args\"` delta type and maintain `end_of_message` boolean to indicate finalization. If args never arrive before `end_of_message` we treat as empty.
Sam: minor nit — I worry about ambiguity between `null` vs `{}` for typed languages. Suggest contract say "absent or empty map = no args" and recommend SDKs expose Option/nullable map. Also add a lint rule in the contract linter.
Alice: does this affect existing stored prompts? e.g., replaying a convo that used the old `payload` nesting. Migration path?
Mira: compatibility plan: accept both shapes on the server side for 3 months. We add a deprecation warning header when the old shape is used. We'll run a canary that logs occurrences and then flip the strict parser later.
Jon: ok. another question re: role nullability — some existing messages have `role: null` for system-inserted content. Are we keeping that?
Mira: yes, we keep `role` nullable for backward compatibility, but strongly recommend explicit roles. Contract text updated to say `role` may be null but clients should treat null as "assistant" only in legacy cases.
Sam: can you add a quick example for streaming order in the PR description? i.e., sample delta sequence: `delta: {tool_call:name}` -> `delta: {event: \"args\", tool_args:{}}` -> `delta: {end_of_message:true}`
Mira: will add. also @deploy-bot can we kick a small canary after merging?
deploy-bot: scheduled canary deployment for refs/heads/feature/pr-4821 to eng-canary at 2026-03-22T02:00:00Z. Will report occurrences to #eng-telemetry.
Alice: thanks. last ask — can someone from client-sdks do a quick pass for typed-languages (go, java, dotnet) and leave comments on the PR?
Sam: I'll take Go and Java. Jon can you do dotnet?
Jon: yup. I'll leave inline comments by EOD.
Mira: thanks all — merging after SDK comments and I/O example added. I'll also create a short confluence note and tag this for the upcoming API contract changelog.
